icFractions -- fractions integral over an affine domain
*******************************************************

  * Usage: 
        icFractions R
  * Inputs:
      * R, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, an affine domain
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, a list of fractions over R,
        generating the integral closure of R, as an R-algebra.

Description
===========

If the integral closure of R has not yet been computed, that computation is
performed first.  No extra computation is then involved to find the fractions.

+------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]/ideal(x^6-z^6-y^2*z^4);|
+------------------------------------------+
|i2 : icFractions R                        |
|                                          |
|       3   2                              |
|      x   x                               |
|o2 = {--, --, x, y, z}                    |
|       2   z                              |
|      z                                   |
|                                          |
|o2 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i3 : R' = integralClosure R               |
|                                          |
|o3 = R'                                   |
|                                          |
|o3 : QuotientRing                         |
+------------------------------------------+
|i4 : gens R'                              |
|                                          |
|o4 = {w   , w   , x, y, z}                |
|       4,0   3,0                          |
|                                          |
|o4 : List                                 |
+------------------------------------------+
|i5 : netList (ideal R')_*                 |
|                                          |
|     +--------------+                     |
|     |         2    |                     |
|o5 = |w   z - x     |                     |
|     | 3,0          |                     |
|     +--------------+                     |
|     |w   z - w   x |                     |
|     | 4,0     3,0  |                     |
|     +--------------+                     |
|     |         2    |                     |
|     |w   x - w     |                     |
|     | 4,0     3,0  |                     |
|     +--------------+                     |
|     | 2      2    2|                     |
|     |w    - y  - z |                     |
|     | 4,0          |                     |
|     +--------------+                     |
+------------------------------------------+

Notice that the $i$-th fraction corresponds to the $i$-th generator of the
integral closure.  For instance, the variable $w_(3,0) = {x^2 \over z}$.

Caveat
======

(a) Currently in Macaulay2, fractions over quotients of polynomial rings do not
have a nice normal form.  In particular, sometimes the fractions are
`simplified' to give much nastier looking fractions. We hope to improve this.

(b) If you want to control the computation of the integral closure via optional
arguments, then make sure you call *note integralClosure(Ring):
integralClosure_lpRing_rp, first, since icFractions does not have optional
arguments.

See also
========

  * *note integralClosure: integralClosure, -- integral closure of an ideal or
    a domain
  * *note icMap: icMap, -- natural map from an affine domain into its integral
    closure

Ways to use icFractions:
========================

  * "icFractions(Ring)"

For the programmer
==================

The object *note icFractions: icFractions, is a *note method function:
(Macaulay2Doc)MethodFunction,.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

