integralClosure(...,Limit=>...) -- do a partial integral closure
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        integralClosure(R, Limit => n)
  * Inputs:
      * n, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, how many steps to perform

Description
===========

The integral closure algorithm proceeds by finding a suitable ideal $J$, and
then computing $Hom_R(J,J)$, and repeating these steps.  This optional argument
limits the number of such steps to perform.

The result is an integral extension, but is not necessarily integrally closed.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y,z]/ideal(x^6-z^6-y^2*z^4-z^3);                               |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R' = integralClosure(R, Variable => symbol t, Limit => 2)               |
|                                                                             |
|o2 = R'                                                                      |
|                                                                             |
|o2 : QuotientRing                                                            |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : trim ideal R'                                                           |
|                                                                             |
