ringFromFractions -- find presentation for f.g. ring
****************************************************

  * Usage: 
        (F,G) = ringFromFractions(H,f)
  * Inputs:
      * H, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a one row matrix over a ring
        $R$
      * f, a *note ring element: (Macaulay2Doc)RingElement,, 
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * Variable => a *note symbol: (Macaulay2Doc)Symbol,, default value "w",
        name of symbol used for new variables
      * Index => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0, the
        starting index for new variables
      * Verbosity => an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, default value 0,
        values up to 6 are implemented. Larger values show more output.
  * Outputs:
      * F, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, $R \rightarrow S$, where
        $S$ is the extension ring of $R$ generated by the fractions $1/f H$
      * G, a *note ring map: (Macaulay2Doc)RingMap,, $frac S \rightarrow frac
        R$, the fractions

Description
===========

Serious restriction: It is assumed that this ring R[1/f H] is an endomorphism
ring of an ideal in $R$.  This means that the Groebner basis, in a product
order, will have lead terms all quadratic monomials in the new variables,
together with other elements which are degree 0 or 1 in the new variables.

+----------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : R = QQ[x,y]/(y^2-x^3)                          |
|                                                    |
|o1 = R                                              |
|                                                    |
|o1 : QuotientRing                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : H = (y * ideal(x,y)) : ideal(x,y)              |
|                                                    |
|                2                                   |
|o2 = ideal (y, x )                                  |
|                                                    |
|o2 : Ideal of R                                     |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : (F,G) = ringFromFractions(((gens H)_{1}), H_0);|
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : S = target F                                   |
|                                                    |
|o4 = S                                              |
|                                                    |
|o4 : QuotientRing                                   |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : F                                              |
|                                                    |
|o5 = map (S, R, {x, y})                             |
|                                                    |
|o5 : RingMap S <-- R                                |
+----------------------------------------------------+
|i6 : G                                              |
|                                                    |
|                           y                        |
|o6 = map (frac R, frac S, {-, x, y})                |
|                           x                        |
|                                                    |
|o6 : RingMap frac R <-- frac S                      |
+----------------------------------------------------+

